/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * filterDescInit
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * filterDescInit()
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * None
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Initialize the filter descriptor software structures
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Build the linked list that holds the filter combination names.
 * Each "filter" is comprised of a name plus two names one of
 * which refers to a filter in filter wheel one while the other picks
 * out a filter in filter wheel two.
 *
 * Not needed when EPICS handles this.
 * 
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * setFilters
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * setFilters(start, rhs, orig)
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * (>) start (char *)
 * (>) rhs (char *)
 * (>) orig (char *)
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Parse a filter "alias" command and store the data.
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Parse each line in the configuration file that is an 'alias'.  Each
 * alias points to two filters names, one in each filter wheel.  These latter
 * associations have been read in by the configuration process prior
 * to reading this configuration file.
 * 
 * format is  alias = "abc" as "kmn" and "rst"
 * or         alias = "abc" as 101 and 205
 * 
 * The numbers are treated as strings, but are included so, if wanted,
 * small numbers can be used to "indicies".
 *
 * Not needed when EPICS handles the alias capability.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * dumpFilters
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * dumpFilters()
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * None
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (void) Returns 'void' and hence has no STATUS value
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Display filter information
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Prints the correspondence between "alias" names and those of
 * the two filters that make up that alias.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
/*
 *+
 * FUNCTION NAME:
 * finishFiltersConfig
 *
 * INVOCATION:
 * finishFiltersConfig()
 *
 * PARAMETERS: (">" input, "!" modified, "<" output)
 * None
 *
 * FUNCTION VALUE:
 * (int) Returns VME_OK (0) or VME_ERROR (1) as status
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Verify filter naming as consistent
 *
 * DESCRIPTION:
 * Check that each of the filter pairs in a composite 'filter' points to
 * a named position on a wheel and that the two named positions are on
 * different wheels.
 *
 * EXTERNAL VARIABLES:
 *
 *
 * PRIOR REQUIREMENTS:
 *
 *
 * DEFICIENCIES:
 *
 *
 * HISTORY:
 * Jul 1, 2001      Initial Version                 (rwolff@noao.edu)
 *
 *-
 */
